We have the equation $\frac{2x-1}{2x+2}=\frac{x-3}{x-1}$. Cross-multiplying and simplifying, we get \begin{align*}
(2x-1)(x-1)&=(2x+2)(x-3)\\
2x^2 - x - 2x + 1 &= 2x^2 + 2x - 3 \cdot 2x - 3 \cdot 2 \\
2x^2 - 3x + 1&=2x^2-4x-6\\
x&=\boxed{-7}
\end{align*}

We have the equation $\frac{3+x}{5+x}=\frac{1+x}{2+x}$. Simplifying, we get \begin{align*}
(3+x)(2+x)&=(5+x)(1+x)\\
6+5x+x^2&=5+6x+x^2\\
x&=\boxed{1}.
\end{align*}

We have that
\begin{align*}
\frac{\csc \theta}{\sin \theta} - \frac{\cot \theta}{\tan \theta} &= \frac{1/\sin \theta}{\sin \theta} - \frac{\cos \theta/\sin \theta}{\sin \theta/\cos \theta} \\
&= \frac{1}{\sin^2 \theta} - \frac{\cos^2 \theta}{\sin^2 \theta} \\
&= \frac{1 - \cos^2 \theta}{\sin^2 \theta} = \frac{\sin^2 \theta}{\sin^2 \theta} = \boxed{1}.
\end{align*}

