source_solution:
Simplify according to the order of operations. \begin{align*}
3!(2^3+\sqrt{9})\div 2 &= 6(8+3)\div 2 \\
&=6(11)\div 2 \\
&=66\div 2\\
&=\boxed{33}.
\end{align*}

We factor and rearrange the terms in the factorials:

\begin{align*}
\frac{3\cdot 5! + 15\cdot 4!}{6!} &= \frac{3\cdot 5! + 3\cdot 5!}{6!} \\
&= \frac{2\cdot 3 \cdot 5!}{6!} \\
&= \frac{6!}{6!} \\
&= \boxed{1}
\end{align*}

To begin, consider the number of ways to arrange the three countries around the circle.  We can consider the English representatives a block, the Germans another block, and the French a third block.  There are $(3-1)!=2$ ways to arrange these three blocks around a circle.  We can also see this by simply drawing the two possible arrangements: [asy]
label("E",(0,0));
label("F",(-.75,-1));
label("G",(.75,-1));
label("E",(3,0));
label("F",(3.75,-1));
label("G",(2.25,-1));
[/asy] Within the English group, there are $3!=6$ ways to arrange the three representatives.  Similarly, there are $4!$ ways to arrange the Germans and $2!$ ways to arrange the French representatives.  Overall, the total number of ways to seat the 9 representatives is: $$2!\times3!\times4!\times2!=2\times6\times24\times2=\boxed{576}$$

We notice that 6! is a common factor of the numerator and denominator and then simplify: \begin{align*}
\frac{7!+8!}{6!+7!} &= \frac{7\cdot6!+8\cdot7\cdot6!}{6!+7\cdot6!} \\
&=\frac{6!(7+8\cdot7)}{6!(1+7)} \\
&=\frac{7+56}{1+7}\\
&=\boxed{\frac{63}{8}}\\
\end{align*}

Cancel before multiplying: \begin{align*}
\frac{14!}{5!9!}&=\frac{14\cdot13\cdot12\cdot11\cdot10\cdot9!}{5\cdot4\cdot3\cdot2\cdot9!} \\
&= \frac{14 \cdot 13 \cdot 12 \cdot 11 \cdot 10}{5 \cdot 4 \cdot 3 \cdot 2} \\
&= \frac{14 \cdot 13 \cdot 12 \cdot 11}{4 \cdot 3} \\
&= 14 \cdot 13 \cdot 11 \\
&= \boxed{2002}
\end{align*}

We do some simplification, taking advantage of the fact that $n! = n\cdot (n-1)!$: \begin{align*}
\frac{9!\cdot 5!\cdot 2!}{8!\cdot 6!} &= \frac{9\cdot 8! \cdot 5! \cdot 2}{8!\cdot 6\cdot 5!}\\
&= \frac{9\cdot 2}{6}\\
&= \boxed{3}.
\end{align*}

