Since $\overline{PA}$ is perpendicular to both $\overline{AB}$ and $\overline{AD}$, the segment $\overline{PA}$ is the altitude from the apex to the base of the pyramid.   To find this length, consider right triangle $PAB$.  Applying the Pythagorean Theorem gives $PA = \sqrt{PB^2 - AB^2} = 15$.

The area of the base is $[ABCD] = (AB)(BC) = 32$, so the volume of the pyramid is $\frac13(32)(15) = \boxed{160}$ cubic units.

