Then $BD = \frac{x}{3/2} = \frac{2x}{3},$ and $CD = \frac{x}{1/2} = 2x,$ so
\[BC = BD + DC = \frac{2x}{3} + 2x = \frac{8x}{3}.\]Since $BC = 32,$ $x = 12.$

Therefore, $[ABC] = \frac{1}{2} \cdot AD \cdot BC = \frac{1}{2} \cdot 12 \cdot 32 = \boxed{192}.$

By the Law of Cosines on triangle $ABC,$
\[\cos A = \frac{10^2 + 10^2 - 12^2}{2 \cdot 10 \cdot 10} = \frac{7}{25}.\]Let $x = AD = DE = CE.$

[asy]
unitsize(0.5 cm);

pair A, B, C, D, E;
real x = 250/39;

A = (0,8);
B = (-6,0);
C = (6,0);
D = interp(A,B,x/10);
E = interp(A,C,(10 - x)/10);

draw(A--B--C--cycle);
draw(D--E);

